On Thursday 13 October 2011 13:34:59 Gioacchino Mazzurco wrote:
> Yesterday I have build an openwrt image with batman adv but i see that this
> version is not complatible with past version, sniffing packets i see batman
> adv v 14 instead of 12
> 
> Now i can update all openwrt nodes but the problem is that some nodes are
> gentoo based, how to see the batman version and in what version of gentoo
> kernel i can find the same as openwrt ?

There is a page which gives a rough overview about the compat versions [1] and 
the download page contains a complete mapping between kernel versions and 
standalone versions. We will _not_ create a separate list of gentoo (or any 
other distribution) patched kernels.

Kind regards,
	Sven

[1] http://www.open-mesh.org/wiki/batman-adv/Compatversion 
[2] http://www.open-mesh.org/wiki/open-mesh/Download
